        },
        "texto": "This question has no pertinence in our times, since, by reason of being shod with iron, our horses do not injure their hoofs by running upon the rock. Horse-shoeing was, however, unknown to the Hebrews, and is of comparatively modern introduction. Bishop Lowth states that the sho…"
      },
      "c-e155ec946cff8ace": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-606",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The divan on which the beds were spread, or the frames on which they rested, were inlaid and ornamented with ivory. Compare the note on “houses of ivory” (Amos 3:15 #604)."
      }
    },
